  "note": "Full unchanged measured source-index geometry, not independent surveys/accuracy ground truth. Full-input production TIN records XY duplicates and automatic edge rejection; no generated/transformed/thinned performance coordinates. Independent archived retained-CPU worker supplies full f32 distance, exact f64 summary and scalar PLY oracles, then terminates before timing. Both builds adopt cached traversal bounds and the same 1 GiB mesh/BVH policy, resident workers, original logical slices, geometry capacities and reservations; experimental query-order cache is disabled. Candidate synchronously borrows imported WASM f64 slice as triples, avoiding another owned XYZ Vec per query batch in fresh/prepared/hinted C2M bindings. The JS-to-WASM input copy and output copying remain; no borrowed input escapes the call, persistent queries or results are retained. Ordinary unsigned prepared CPU calls are measured; hints, fresh BVH and signed calls receive parity checks but no performance claim. All searches, Morton ordering, guessed triangles, stack reset, exact geometry/distance arithmetic, join/summaries and request policy are unchanged. Avoided payload allocation/copy is 24 bytes per point per batch; this is not measured peak process memory. One excluded first pair, five alternating warm-up pairs and ten alternating timed pairs compare separate archived/current production contexts. Timed geometry misses, query-order hits, fallback, layout/budget mismatch or output differences fail. Whole unsigned RPC includes copies/transfers, ordering/search, join/summaries/arrays. Loading/meshing/startup/first observations/warmups/export/parity/cleanup excluded. Eleven source files, script/artifacts/inputs/manifest/original PCD checked before/after. No builds/tests/scans/edits alongside timing. All losses/spikes retained; clocks/power/scheduling/GC/other apps/code layout/pages uncontrolled. No isolated search/native/signed/GPU speedup claim. No GPU dispatch/model identifiers collected."
